1378969200", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 7, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "11938814", "author": {"steamid": "76561198110362149", "personaname": "Ray G.", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/bigTownTP/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 5, "playtime_forever": 3318, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 872, "last_played": 1451694573, "avatar": "2d5672fb551ad5f6c7f41d627ae605f1155fc493"}, "language": "english", "review": "I recommend playing Dayz first, as the community taught me all the tips and tricks about playing Arma or an Arma based mod. When I first picked up Arma 3, even after staring at the config screen, I was still confused and got stuck repeatedly. With Dayz it kinda progresses you from how to change from first person to third, shooting, then figuring out how far your target is away so you can compensate for it. Arma doesnt really teach you that right away, thats way I was lost. Also, the campaign in arma (what ive played of it) is pretty cool, aswell as the multiplayer, but its big hitter is definetly the mods. Battle Royal, Atlas Life, theyre all great and super fun, as well as the community. I definetly recommend you get this game as there are endless posibilities.", "timestamp_created": 1409513121, "timestamp_updated": 1409513121, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.502074718475341797", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1378969200", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "11936377", "author": {"steamid": "76561198027437871", "personaname": "Lulu", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/HE_ZUCC_ME/", "num_games_owned": 426, "num_reviews": 18, "playtime_forever": 42182, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 15313, "last_played": 1745607504, "avatar": "ba5